> Compare executed work with an explicitly hypothetical model

The old work plot simulated a variable-width trial-subtraction/restoration loop.
That differed from both canonical routines, which process64 bits. More
importantly, native restoring_divide compares first and subtracts only when the
remainder fits. It executes no restoration additions. Its actual subtraction
count equals the quotient’s popcount; failed comparisons perform no add-back.
Non-restoring executes64 add/subtract operations plus zero or one final
correction.

The original six dividends with divisor13 remain, and their effective dividend
bit widths identify the fixtures. The first panel compares actual selected
arithmetic counts. The second explicitly models a different classical circuit
that trial-subtracts on every one of64 stages and adds back after each failed
trial:64+hypothetical_restores. That modeled count is derived from actual failed
comparisons, not mislabeled as executed software. These are selected operations,
excluding comparisons, shifts, guards, loop control and formatting; no timing or
CPU instruction cost conclusion follows.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nonrestoring_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, r_actual, n_actual, hypothetical;
    std::print("| original dividend | bit width | actual restoring subtractions | actual restoring " "additions | actual nonrestoring add/subtracts incl final | hypothetical trial/restore model " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto n : dm::algorithms::division_work_dividends()) {
        auto r =
            dm::algorithms::restoring_division_analyze(n, 13), a =
            dm::algorithms::non_restoring_division_analyze(n, 13);
        x.push_back(std::bit_width(n));
        r_actual.push_back(r.subtractions + r.additions);
        n_actual.push_back(a.subtractions + a.additions);
        hypothetical.push_back(r.bit_steps + r.hypothetical_restores);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, std::bit_width(n),
                   r.subtractions, r.additions, a.subtractions + a.additions,
                   r.bit_steps + r.hypothetical_restores);
    }
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, r_actual, "compare/subtract", {36, 105, 172}, 5).points(
        x, n_actual, "non-restoring", {192, 59, 50}, 4).title(
        "Actual selected arithmetic").x_label("dividend bit width;64 stages each").y_label("executed add/subtracts");
    layout.add(p);
    auto q = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    q.points(x, hypothetical, "trial/restore model", {124, 58, 237}, 5).points(
        x, n_actual, "non-restoring actual", {192, 59, 50}, 4).title(
        "Hypothetical circuit comparison").x_label("dividend bit width;64 stages each").y_label("modeled or actual add/subtracts");
    layout.add(q);
    layout.size(1300, 650).fit_panels().save_svg("build/nonrestoring_work.svg");
}
```
