> Zero dividend, equal operands and the legacy zero-divisor sentinel

A zero dividend with nonzero divisor still follows64 bit stages and returns
exact zero. Equal full-width operands return1 remainder0. The historical
divisor-zero entry point returns{0,0,0}; this is an explicit sentinel, not a
defined quotient. Analyzed and traced calls expose valid_divisor=false so the
report never treats that sentinel as an arithmetic result. Compatibility with
existing callers and tests is retained.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nonrestoring_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto max = std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();
    std::vector<std::pair<std::uint64_t, std::uint64_t>> pairs{{0, 13},
                                                               {13, 13},
                                                               {max, max},
                                                               {5, 0}};
    std::vector<std::string> names{"zero dividend", "equal", "full-width equal",
                                   "zero divisor"};
    std::vector<double> steps;
    std::print("| control | valid divisor | actual quotient/sentinel | actual remainder/sentinel | actual " "bit stages |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < pairs.size(); ++i) {
        auto[n, d] = pairs[i];
        auto r = dm::algorithms::non_restoring_division_analyze(n, d);
        steps.push_back(r.bit_steps);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", names[i], r.valid_divisor,
                   r.result.quotient, r.result.remainder, r.bit_steps);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(steps, names, "actual stages");
    p.title("Non-restoring controls: fixed64 stages or explicit sentinel").x_label("original unsigned operands").y_label("actual bit stages").save_svg("build/nonrestoring_controls.svg");
}
```
