| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| zero dividend | true | 0 | 0 | 64 |
| equal | true | 1 | 0 | 64 |
| full-width equal | true | 1 | 0 | 64 |
| zero divisor | false | 0 | 0 | 0 |
\image(figures/nonrestoring_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual fixed-stage work and the explicitly invalid zero-divisor sentinel.)
\alttext(Zero or equal dividends are valid64-stage divisions; divisor zero has no mathematical quotient and performs no stages.)

> Storage and exact history

Nonzero-divisor work is O(64), with constant driver state. Restoring and
non-restoring traces own their original operands, actual results and64
fixed-size bit records. Complete logical policies are5+steps and6+steps
respectively, the latter including a final-correction record. Defaults1000000,
zero disables, pre-admitted before arithmetic/history allocation. Zero-divisor
traces retain only their fixed sentinel metadata. Exact signed magnitudes use
two unsigned64-bit words plus sign; decimal formatting and rounded plotting
conversion are outside arithmetic counters.

The original intent—carrying overshoots instead of immediate restoration—remains
visible in actual records. The corrected work study explains the separate
software and circuit models without claiming saved adds that this native
comparison-first restoring implementation never executed.

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes75 CTest cases,22 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,122 compiled and executed public examples,538/538 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
arbitrary-precision arithmetic verifies69365 captured division records
with656460 checks; native independent polynomial, geometry, finite-range, graph,
ranking and callback checks cover the remaining producers. Frozen valid-input
comparisons preserve Neville recurrences, Newton result/callback paths, complete
byte encodings, switch routes and NSGA-II complete objective-call
sequences/final fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten byte-identical installed
development headers compile independently; an installed-header native consumer
links and runs. All40 complete programs execute, and40 native figures have been
visually reviewed; HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed rows/prose and
identical image bytes. Checks are scoped native checks, not an installation
claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-254-263/`.
